  "memo": "R03 holds: the GB-issued card was used from a US IP and AVS failed. Card is the only adverse family; no other rule holds, and no household exception is needed. No earlier outcome settles the order, and no verification has run. Legitimate use of a foreign-issued card with an address mismatch remains plausible; longstanding card use does not establish the current purchaser's identity. Recommend needs_check under FP-2 §6.6(b), implemented as a hold for id_check. This is the only required check and directly tests account identity and cardholder authentication. A pass clears the order; a failure requires decline without Linkage."
